{number: 47}
{title: Blessed Assurance, Jesus Is Mine}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Blessed assurance, [F] Jesus is [C] mine!
O what a [Am] foretaste of [D7] glory di-[G] vine!
[C] Heir of salvation, [F] purchase of [C] God,
Born of His [Dm] Spirit, [G7] washed in His [C] blood.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
This is my [C] story, this is my [F] song,
Praising my [C] Savior [Am] all the day [G] long;
This is my [C] story, this is my [F] song,
Praising my [C] Savior [G7] all the day [C] long.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Perfect submission, [F] perfect de-[C] light,
Visions of [Am] rapture now [D7] burst on my [G] sight;
[C] Angels descending, [F] bring from a-[C] bove
Echoes of [Dm] mercy, [G7] whispers of [C] love.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Perfect submission, [F] all is at [C] rest,
I in my [Am] Savior am [D7] happy and [G] blest;
